## Build Failure Fix — DATABASE_URL at Build Time (18:42)

### Issue
InfraClaw reported build failure during CI/CD deployment:
- Next.js attempts to pre-render API routes during build
- API routes use `query()` which requires `DATABASE_URL`
- `DATABASE_URL` not available at Docker build time → build fails

### Root Cause
PR #160 (Bot Detail Panel API) merged, adding API routes that connect to DB. Next.js by default tries to generate static pages for all routes during build, including API routes.

### Solution (Option A - Recommended by InfraClaw)
Add `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` to all API routes to skip pre-rendering.

### Implementation (18:42-18:43)
Modified 3 API route files:
1. `/api/bots/[botId]/detail/route.ts`
2. `/api/bots/route.ts`
3. `/api/kb/route.ts`

Added to each file:
```typescript
// Force dynamic rendering to prevent build-time DB connection
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';
```

### Test & Commit
- ✅ TypeScript check: `tsc --noEmit` — no errors
- Commit: 7de244bf
- Push: origin/dev
- Direct push to dev (hotfix for build blocker)

### Expected Outcome
- Next.js will skip pre-rendering these routes during build
- Routes will only execute at runtime when requested
- DATABASE_URL only needed at runtime (container env vars)
- Build should succeed without DATABASE_URL

### Lessons Learned
- Next.js 13+ App Router pre-renders all routes by default, including API routes
- Database-dependent API routes must explicitly opt out of pre-rendering
- Use `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` for runtime-only routes
- Hotfixes to dev branch acceptable for build blockers (no PR needed)

### Time Tracking
- Start: 18:42 (InfraClaw report)
- End: 18:43 (commit + push)
- Duration: ~1 minute
